# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env example for `lambda-rag rules synopsize`
#
# This is an AUTHORING-TIME tool. It walks a ruleset.json once, asks a
# OpenRouter model (openai/gpt-5.6-luna) to write a one-sentence plain-English
# summary of each rule's intent, and bakes the result into the rule's
# Metadata["synopsis"] field. Runtime evaluation never calls an LLM, so
# lambda-rag's determinism guarantee is preserved.
#
# Set OPENROUTER_API_KEY in your shell or secret manager. Do not commit it.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values, OR export them inline.
# The --model CLI flag overrides OPENROUTER_MODEL.

OPENROUTER_API_KEY=<set-in-shell-or-secret-manager>
OPENROUTER_MODEL=openai/gpt-5.6-luna

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Usage
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   lambda-rag rules synopsize \
#     --ruleset out/dev-full/policies-ruleset.json \
#     --out     out/dev-full/policies-ruleset.json \
#     --cache-dir out/.synopsis-cache
#
# Idempotent: rules that already have Metadata["synopsis"] are skipped
# unless --force is passed. Cache is content-hashed so re-runs after a
# rule edit only re-call the LLM for the changed rule.
